  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 324 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nDuring the long term, Monday into Friday, high pressure \ncontinues to dominate the region leaving afternoon highs in the 90s. \nWith the high pressure expected to go through a slight evolution and \npotential suppression, high temperatures may be held in the mid 90s, \nas opposed to the upper 90s to 105 range seen of lately. Still above \naverage for this time of year. Also, the high pressure over the \nregion is expected to limit PoPs despite decent H7 moisture staying \nin place. With weak looking synoptics the current forecast only has \nslight chance to chance PoPs returning Wed night, across the \nnorthern combined Panhandles. With the H5 high expected to shift \nwest of the Panhandles Thursday, weak northwest flow may contribute \nto some shower/thunderstorm activity. At this time the NBM is only \ngiving a slight chance PoPs for Thu/Thu night but is covering more \nof the combined Panhandles.",
